{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#915","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#915","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#915\",\"parent_revision\":\"41cdf796d9908cf367aa2bad0f30643d8564ed3002f26376fdd6cc07bb918602\",\"root_revision\":\"41cdf796d9908cf367aa2bad0f30643d8564ed3002f26376fdd6cc07bb918602\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPlugin reference docs and SKILL.md files now have {OWNER/REPO} placeholders that require agents to do a lookup step. The MCP tools already handle repo discovery internally via discover_repo() \u2014 docs should use MCP tool instructions (which are repo-transparent) instead of raw commands with placeholders. Goal: zero extra steps for agents in other repos. The plugin should work without the agent needing to discover or pass the repo.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an agent reads plugin docs in any repository, it can invoke MCP tools directly without first resolving a `{OWNER/REPO}` value. The MCP tools call `discover_repo()` internally; the docs do not need to surface repo coordinates.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nEach occurrence falls into one of three replacement patterns:\\n\\n1. **CLI flag example** (`-R {OWNER/REPO}`) in migration/README docs: replace with a note that the MCP tool handles repo discovery automatically \u2014 no `-R` flag needed.\\n2. **Code block comment** (`# OWNER/REPO is discovered dynamically via discover_repo()`): already correct framing \u2014 verify comment is accurate, not a call to action.\\n3. **Example output URL** (`https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/issues/59`): replace with a description of the URL shape or omit the placeholder entirely, since the URL is constructed internally by the MCP tool.\\n4. **GitHub URL in template** (`https://github.com/{OWNER/REPO}/milestone/N`): replace with a note to retrieve the URL from the MCP tool response rather than constructing it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -r 'OWNER/REPO' plugins/development-harness/ --include='*.md'` returns zero matches.\\n2. Every previously affected file still accurately describes the MCP tool call pattern for the operation it documents (no content removed without replacement).\\n3. `uv run prek run --files <each modified file>` exits 0 (no lint regressions).\\n4. The `work-backlog-item` and `backlog` skills load without broken cross-references: verify with `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/` and `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md` \u2014 migration context, already documents MCP-first approach |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/github-integration.md` \u2014 already has correct `discover_repo()` note on line 3 |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 already has correct comment on line 306 |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 7 files, 11 string replacements, each replacement is a localized text edit with a clear pattern. No logic changes, no schema changes. Lint validation is the primary quality gate.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Summary\\n\\nGoal: Replace `{OWNER/REPO}` placeholder strings in plugin reference docs and SKILL.md files with repo-transparent MCP tool call instructions, eliminating the extra lookup step agents currently face in other repos.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 scope, affected files, and replacement approach are all derivable from the codebase.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**11 actionable occurrences in 7 files** (confirmed via grep 2026-03-30):\\n\\n| File | Count | Context |\\n|------|-------|---------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md` | 3 | CLI flag docs, example YAML, add command example |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/github-integration.md` | 3 | Comment in code block, example output URL |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` | 1 | Example invocation URL |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/validation-plan.md` | 1 | Repo discovery note |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` | 1 | Comment in code block |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` | 1 | CLI sync example |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/templates/milestone-archive.md` | 1 | GitHub milestone URL template |\\n\\n**Out of scope (intentional template variables, not lookup placeholders):**\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/readme-badger/` \u2014 `{owner}/{repo}` is badge URL template syntax, not a step requiring resolution\\n- `.claude/skills/daily-releases/SKILL.md` \u2014 `-R OWNER/REPO` is CLI flag documentation, correct as-is\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 `{owner}/{repo}` in `gh api` URL templates is standard gh CLI syntax\\n- `research/` directory \u2014 documentation of external tools, not agent-facing instructions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-20T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **replace {owner/repo} placeholders in plugin docs with transparent mcp tool calls** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-20T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-03-20: user pointed out placeholders create extra work for agents in other repos\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"943d8acde6fd4c76bc75a7c81153d504d577f69b56b94408d2118ef3d5de2c0c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEg6g\"}"}